The conditioned rerun exposed a deeper issue, so I’m stopping the build rather than tuning around it. Once one matching is set to the obvious alternating phase, a random choice of the other mask is Hamiltonian roughly 25–40% of the time at tested shipping-scale dimensions. That is a structure-aware guessing attack, not a planting artefact, and it defeats both Track A and the intended Track B family. I’m preserving the attempted module under the required rejected filename and documenting the measured failure.
